#+TITLE: SNCF native ARX fails during AutoCAD startup in SSH diagnostics
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation

* Evidence
On 2026-11-02 at20:20 UTC, isolated SSH diagnostic AutoCAD PID28608 exits
before READY. Windows Application events1000/1001 identify
sncfoutilsarx64.arx version1.0.0.1, offset0x10379, exception0xC0000409,
BEX64, fast-fail parameter2. A matching acad.exe.28608.dmp exists.
The executable used in the first diagnostic was2.3.94 (MR !476), copied
from a reused CI workspace, not the intended MR !507 build. That run is
not qualification evidence for !507. A separately built2.3.91 also fails
before READY under SSH. No owned COM identity was captured before failure;
there is no CAD process left afterwards.

* Investigation
Keep this startup failure distinct from the earlier post-test0xC0000005
and variable0x...BABE exits. Compare the normal GitLab runner environment
with SSH and preserve the matching WER report and dump. Do not attribute
all AutoCAD failures to one module without matching process evidence.

** Further isolated native controls (2026-11-02)
On pfenny, starting from the existing unnamed AutoCAD profile avoids the
early SNCF ARX failure in this trial. Control loading alone exposes neither
EPURE API. Explicit AcadDoc.lsp/S::STARTUP after opening the job DWG restores
both APIs. The modified private DWG is discarded with its SHA256 unchanged.
AutoCAD nevertheless exits 0x0141BABE without forced cleanup, WER event or dump.
A preceding cold-profile run with neither EPURE API loaded exits 0x013CBABE.
Therefore BABE alone does not establish that EPURE caused the exit; its meaning
remains unclassified and the strict lifecycle gate continues to fail it.
ProcDump attached to the exact owned process observed no C0000005 in these
two trials. Earlier real C0000005 and startup C0000409 evidence is retained.
The startup timeout left PID9584 recorded by this diagnostic launcher; its
67 MB dump was preserved before terminating that exact PID after verifying
creation time and owner. User profiles were restored to Epure and temporary
scheduled tasks removed. No generic shutdown experiment is shipped.
